### Azure Function App – HTTP requests
### If "Send Request" doesn't appear: click "Plain Text" in the status bar (bottom-right) and choose "HTTP".
### Use with VS Code REST Client. Replace {{baseUrl}} and {{functionKey}}.
### Local: baseUrl = http://localhost:7071   Azure: baseUrl = https://<your-app>.azurewebsites.net
### Get function key: Azure Portal → Function App → App keys (default or per-function key)

@baseUrl = https://assignment-for-tripple-az.azurewebsites.net


#please paste the jobId that was received from the POST endpoint 
#(maybe wait a few seconds before the worker actuall takes over the job) but it works I swear :)!!!!
@receivedJobId = 
###############################################################################
# RequestImageGeneration – start a new image generation job (POST)
# Returns 202 with jobId and status "QUEUED". Use jobId with GetJobStatus.
###############################################################################
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/RequestImageGeneration?code={{functionKeyRequestJob}}
Content-Type: application/json

###############################################################################
# RequestImagesFunction – welcome / health (GET or POST)
###############################################################################
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/GetJobStatus?jobId={{receivedJobId}}&code={{functionKeyGetJob}}
